ugust 29, titled “A dream derailed”, which highlighted the project’s setbacks, including contractor exits, land acquisition issues, and lack of coordination between agencies. “I have discussed the matter thoroughly today with officials. I will take this up with Railway Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw soon. I recently travelled by suburban trains in Chennai and Kolkata and observed its success there. Yes, I agree that Bengaluru’s project has been delayed considerably,” Mr. Somanna said at a press conference after the review meeting. He added that a dedicated review with State government officials and MPs would be held within the next 20 to 25 days to explore whether the Railways should directly take over the project from the Karnataka Rail Infrastructure Development Company (K-RIDE) and implement it. P.C. Mohan, MP for Bangalore Central, reiterated that the State government’s lack of urgency in land acquisition was a major hurdle, urging the Railways to take full control of the project. Speaking to The Hindu, Mr. Mohan said, “The delay is happening because of land acquisition. The suburban rail is badly needed for Bengaluru, but the state government is not showing enough interest. That is why I requested the Railways to take over the entire project and implement it directly.” Sanctioned in October 2020, the 148-km network was originally expected to be completed in phases by October 2023, well before the final deadline of October 2026. When Prime Minister Narendra Modi laid the foundation stone in June 2022, he assured Bengaluru citizens that the long-pending project would be delivered within 40 months, finally ending a four-decade wait.\\n However, progress has been sluggish. In a major setback earlier this month, Larsen &amp; Toubro (L&amp;T) terminated its contracts for two corridors Chikkabanavara to Bennigenahalli and Heelalige to Rajankunte citing project delays and unresolved issues.\\n Published - August 29, 2025 10:08 pm IST\\n\\nTitle: The Hindu Impact: V. Somanna promises review to f…\\nAuthor: system\\nPublished Date: 2025-08-30T00:00:00.000Z\\nURL: https://indiarailinfo.com/news/post/the-hindu-imp…\\nText: The Hindu Impact: V. Somanna promises review to fast-track Bengaluru Suburban Railway Project On Friday, August 29th, a review meeting concerning Bengaluru's Suburban Railway Project was held. V. Somanna, MoS for Railways, committed to a separate meeting with senior officials and the Karnataka government to address project delays. This response followed The Hindu's 'Spotlight' report on August 29th, which criticized setbacks including contractor exits,... more... Friday, August 29 ko, Bengaluru ke Suburban Railway Project par ek review meeting hui. Railway ke MoS, V. Somanna ne senior officials aur Karnataka government ke saath ek alag meeting karne ka waada kiya, project mein ho rahi delays ko address karne ke liye. Yeh assurance The Hindu ke 'Spotlight' report,... more...\\n\\nTitle: Crores spent, but flyovers in Bengaluru going now…\\nAuthor: DHNS\\nPublished Date: 2025-08-29T00:00:00.000Z\\nURL: https://www.deccanherald.com/india/karnataka/beng…\\nText: Many flyover projects are in limbo, but that is not stopping us from planning more DHNS Last Updated : 29 August 2025, 22:17 IST ADVERTISEMENT Follow Us : Comments ADVERTISEMENT Published 29 August 2025, 22:17 IST Bengaluru Bengaluru news Specials Point Blank Follow us on : Follow Us\\n\\nTitle: Mangalore to Bengaluru Trains | Book from 4 Train…\\nAuthor: \\nPublished Date: 2025-08-30T00:00:00.000Z\\nURL: https://www.ixigo.com/by-train-rail/mangalore-to-…\\nText: # Mangalore to Bengaluru Trains\\n\\n![origin-icon](https://www.ixigo.com/rt-train/pc/img/originPrimary.svg)\\n\\nFrom\\n\\n![swap-icon](https://www.ixigo.com/rt-train/pc/img/swap.svg)\\n\\n![destination-icon](https://www.ixigo.com/rt-train/pc/img/destinationPrimary.svg)\\n\\nTo\\n\\nDeparture Date\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n## 4 Trains from Mangalore to Bengaluru\\n\\n[मंगलौर से बंगलोर के लिए ट्रेन (हिंदी में देखें )