/sunday-read/articlelist/20970381.cms)\\n- [You](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/you/articlelist/20970332.cms)\\n- [Code 560](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/code-560/articlelist/21676784.cms)\\n- [Others](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/columns-views-pet-puja-queer-issues-dialogue-gardening-greenskeeper-opinions/articlelist/20970746.cms)\\n- [Views](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/views/articlelist/21167504.cms)\\n- [Food](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/food/articlelist/20970329.cms)\\n- [Teen Spirit](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/teen-spirit/articlelist/20970318.cms)\\n- [Blogs](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/opinion/blogs/blogview/20970733.cms)\\n\\n[Others](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/section/20970300.cms)\\n\\n- [Letters to the Editor](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/letters-to-the-editor)\\n- [Sci-Tech](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/sci-tech)\\n- [Leisure](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/leisure/articlelist/20970325.cms)\\n- [Trending Today](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/trending-today/articlelist/20970324.cms)\\n- [Lit.Mus 2014](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/others/lit-mus-2014/articlelist/20970312.cms)\\n\\n- [Home](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com)/\\n- [Bangalore](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/bangalore)/\\n- [Other](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/bangalore/others)/\\n- Stepping out in your best jeans? Be careful\\n\\n# Stepping out in your best jeans? Be careful\\n\\nBySridhar VivanSridhar Vivan/ Updated: May 8, 2023, 06:00 IST\\n\\n- [Facebook](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Twitter](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Linkedin](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Email](javascript:void(0);)\\n\\n- _Share_\\n\\n- [Facebook](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Twitter](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Linkedin](javascript:void(0);)\\n- [Email](javascript:void(0);)\\n\\n[Print this article](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/articleshowprint/100057736.cms?prtpage=1)\\n\\n[Reduce font size](javascript:void(0);)\\n\\n[Increase font size](javascript:void(0);)\\n\\n![Stepping out in your best jeans? Be careful](https://static.toiimg.com/thumb/imgsize-149420,msid-100057729,width-400,resizemode-4/100057729.jpg)\\n\\nAccording to experts, jeans can trap heat and sweat, leading to a buildup of bacteria and fungi in summer\\n\\n**City dermatologists urge citizens to be cautious about infections that can result from wearing tight jeans during summer season; recommend baggy or cotton clothes**\\n\\nWhile many prefer to wear their jeans throughout the year, doctors say that it is better to avoid them in the summer when there is an increase in temperature.\\n\\nDr Sudheendra G Udbalker (Consultant Dermatology, Fortis Hospital, Bannerghatta Road) told Bangalore Mirror that in summer, wearing tight jeans could lead to discomfort and fungal infections due to the heat and moisture they trap.\\n\\n“Fungi thrive in warm, moist environments and can cause skin infections such as athlete’s foot, jock itch, and ringworm. These infections can be prevented by wearing loose-fitting, breathable clothing made from natural fibres like cotton or linen. It’s also important to change out of sweaty clothing as soon as possible, keep the skin clean and dry, and seek medical treatment if an infection develops,” he said.\\n\\nRemember to stay hydrated, avoid prolonged sun exposure during the hottest parts of the day, and take steps to protect your skin and overall health during summer, he advised.\\n\\nFurthermore, Dr Shireen Furtado (Consultant - Medical and Cosmetic Dermatology, Aster CMI Hospital) said that summer clothing choices should be chosen carefully.\\n\\n“Particularly, wearing jeans can negatively affect our skin’s health. While they may be a fashion staple, they can also trap heat and sweat, leading to a buildup of bacteria and fungi and ultimately leading to skin irritation, rashes, and even infections like tinea or ringworm. It is important to note that the fabric of the jeans, as well as their fit, can also have an impact on the skin. To minimise the risk of skin irritation and other issues, I recommend that individuals choose breathable, lightweight fabrics such as cotton, linen, or rayon instead of denim,” she said.\\n\\nLoose-fitting clothing can also be helpful in promoting air circulation and reducing the buildup of heat and sweat. If you must wear jeans, try to limit the amount of time you spend in them and choose a lighter wash of denim to reduce heat retention. Also, make sure to keep your skin clean and dry, and avoid wearing tight-fitting undergarments, as they can exacerbate skin irritation, she explained.\\n\\nOther dermatologists added that, though both men and women wear jeans, there is an occlusion of the area underneath the jeans, especially in the groin region and also in the rest of the thigh, which causes various skin conditions.\\n\\nAccording to Dr Anagha Samarth, Consultant Dermatologist, SPARSH Hospital, these skin conditions can be quite uncomfortable and need treatment if aggravated or do not come down by physical measures. As an alternative to jeans, especially in summer due to the hot and humid climate, it is recommended to wear baggy clothes or cotton clothes. Also, it is best to avoid synthetic. “If you are wearing jeans it is better to wear something that is airy,” she said.\\n\\n**Infections in summer**\\n\\n_**• Jock itch is a common fungal infection that lasts throughout the summer in a few patients. This fungal infection is usually present in the groin area and the buttock area. When there is occlusion, there is excessive sweating, and this humid environment is a growth medium for the fungus.**_\\n\\n_**• Miliaria is commonly known as a heat rash or prickly rash. This skin condition is usually seen in hot and humid climates in the summer due to the blockage or inflammation of sweat ducts.**_\\n\\n_**• Folliculitis is an inflammation or infection of the hair follicle. It is seen as a red rash but is more discrete. It is present around the hair follicle itself.**_\\n\\nGALLERIES [View more photos](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photolist/22143713.cms)\\n\\n- [![Aero India 2021: 13th edition of air show begins today](https://static.toiimg.com/photo/62986185.cms)](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/photos-13th-edition-of-aero-india-2021-/aero-india-2021-13th-edition-of-air-show-begins-today/photostory/80666465.cms) [Aero India 2021: 13th edition of air show begins today](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/photos-13th-edition-of-aero-india-2021-/aero-india-2021-13th-edition-of-air-show-begins-today/photostory/80666465.cms)\\n- [![Pedestrians Only!](https://static.toiimg.com/photo/62986185.cms)](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/bengaluru-church-street-comes-alive-on-sundays/pedestrians-only/photostory/79739597.cms) [Pedestrians Only!](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/bengaluru-church-street-comes-alive-on-sundays/pedestrians-only/photostory/79739597.cms)\\n- [![PM lays foundation stone of new Parliament building](https://static.toiimg.com/photo/62986185.cms)](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/everything-you-need-to-know-about-the-new-parliament-building/pm-lays-foundation-stone-of-new-parliament-building/photostory/79679667.cms) [PM lays foundation stone of new Parliament building](https://bangaloremirror.indiatimes.com/photos/news/everything-you-need-to-know-about-the-new-parliament-building/pm-lays-foundation-stone-of-new-parliament-building/photostory/79679667.cms)\\n\\nMost Popular\\n\\n- Most Read\\n- Most commented\\n\\n[![Bengaluru property owners urge BBMP to extend 5% tax rebate](https://static.toiimg.com/thumb/62986185.cms)Bengaluru property owners urge BBMP to ...\\\\\\nBengaluru property owners urge BBMP to extend 5% tax rebate](https://bangaloremirror.india